10
00:34:17,142 --> 00:34:23,142
Mean Girls is a 2004 American teen comedy film produced by Lorne Michaels
and directed by Mark Waters from a screenplay by Tina Fey.

11
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
The film stars Lindsay Lohan in the lead role, with Rachel McAdams, Tim
Meadows, Ana Gasteyer, Amy Poehler, and Fey in supporting roles.

12
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
The plot centers on Cady Heron (Lohan), a naïve teenager who transfers to an
American high school after years of homeschooling in Africa.

13
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
Cady quickly befriends outcasts Janis and Damian (Lizzy Caplan and Daniel Franzese), with the trio forming a plan to
exact revenge on Regina George (McAdams), the leader of an envied clique known as "the Plastics".

14
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Fey conceived the idea for Mean Girls after reading Rosalind
Wiseman's 2002 self-help book Queen Bees and Wannabes.

15
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
The book describes female high school social cliques, school
bullying, and the resulting damaging effect on teenagers.

16
00:54:51,428 --> 00:54:57,428
Fey also drew from her own experience at Upper Darby High School, in Upper Darby
Township, Pennsylvania, as an inspiration for some of the film's concepts.

17
00:58:17,142 --> 00:58:23,142
Principal photography for Mean Girls took place
from September 2003 to November 2003.

18
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
Although the film is set in the Chicago suburb of Evanston, Illinois,
shooting took place primarily in Toronto, Ontario, Canada.

19
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
During post-production, editing was completed by Wendy Greene
Bricmont and the score was composed by Rolfe Kent.

20
01:08:34,285 --> 01:08:40,285
Mean Girls premiered at the Cinerama Dome in Los Angeles on April 19, 2004, and was
theatrically released in the United States on April 30, 2004, by Paramount Pictures.

21
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It was a box office success, grossing $130.1 million
against a production budget of $17–18 million.

22
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
The film received positive reviews from critics, who praised Waters' direction, Fey's script, its humor, and the performances; especially
lauded was Lohan's acting, which earned several accolades, including two MTV Movie Awards and three Teen Choice Awards.

23
01:18:51,428 --> 01:18:57,428
In 2021, Lohan's performance was included in The New Yorker's list
of the best movie performances of the 21st century.

24
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
A made-for-TV sequel, Mean Girls 2, premiered on ABC Family in January 2011.

25
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
Mean Girls also spawned various adaptations, including a stage musical, which premiered on
Broadway in March 2018, with a film adaptation released in January 2024.

26
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, illinois,
female friendship, bullying, coming of age.

27
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
